Run the devcontainer privileged, not under sysbox

Sysbox is no longer required to run systemd and nested container
engines in the devcontainer; plain runc with --privileged works both
locally and on stock GitHub runners. This drops the sysbox install
from CI and the sysbox requirement from the contributor docs.

Under plain runc, nested container storage cannot live on the pod's
own overlayfs root (the kernel refuses overlay-upon-overlay), so
/var/lib/containers and /var/lib/docker each get a named volume, both
in devcontainer.json (keyed per pod via devcontainerId) and in
ci/run-pipeline.sh. The image also masks getty.target, since a
privileged pod sees the host's VT devices, and overrides podman's
tmpfiles entry so docker-group members can reach the rootful socket.
